course: dictionary
lesson: 5173
title: Isograms: no repeated letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An isogram is a word in which no letter appears more than once. The word comes from iso, meaning equal, and gram, meaning letter. To check a word, look at each letter and ask: does this letter appear again anywhere else?
explain: Take «dog». D, o and g each appear once, so dog is an isogram. Now try «letter». The t appears twice and the e appears twice, so letter is not an isogram. Puzzle players check words like this all the time.
explain: Look at the example: «"Uncopyrightable" has 15 letters and not one of them repeats; a word with no repeated letters is called an isogram.» Long words can be isograms too, as long as no letter repeats.
explain: On a map, isogram means something different. It is a line joining places that have the same value, such as the same temperature or height. Isotherms, which join places with the same temperature, and contour lines, which join places with the same height, are both kinds of isograms.
fact: An isogram is a word with no repeated letters.
fact: «Dog» and «planet» are isograms, because no letter in them appears twice.
fact: «Uncopyrightable» is a long isogram with 15 letters.
fact: In geography, an isogram is a line on a map joining places with the same value.
fact: Isotherms and contour lines are kinds of isograms.
exercise: Is «dog» an isogram? | No, it has only three letters | *Yes, no letter appears twice | No, the letter o is in it
exercise: Which of these is an isogram? | committee | *planet | bookkeeper | letter
exercise: On a weather map, what is an isotherm? | A line showing the highest mountain | A word with no repeated letters | A road between two towns | *A line joining places with the same temperature
test: Why is «uncopyrightable» an isogram? | Because it has 15 letters | Because it has a y in it | *Because no letter in it appears more than once
test: Which word is NOT an isogram? | *banana | planet | dog | uncopyrightable
exam: Which of these best describes an isogram? | A word with more than ten letters | *A word in which no letter appears more than once | A word that rhymes with another word | A line on a map joining places with the same height only
